[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2633600914","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101990#issuecomment-2633600914","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101990","id":2633600914,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6c-Y-S","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-04T11:16:08Z","updated_at":"2025-02-04T11:19:40Z","body":"`ViewportTexture` is a dynamic texture, but is usually used in a fixed position (need to set `viewport_path`), like a monitor, except for the **default** one, which is the one obtained by `get_viewport().get_texture()`. The **default** one is like bound to the `Viewport`, it is not fixed (`viewport_path` is not set). \n\nSince the content is dynamic, scripts are free, and resources are passed by reference, the default one is usually used in scripts, but it seems unnecessary to duplicate it.\n\nIf you want to get a screenshot of a specific frame, use `get_image()`. If you want to use it fixedly, you need to set `viewport_path` manually.\n\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2633600914/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3577841504","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101990#issuecomment-3577841504","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101990","id":3577841504,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VQYdg","user":{"login":"Nallebeorn","id":7013489,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTM0ODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7013489?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn","html_url":"https://github.com/Nallebeorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-25T22:24:35Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T22:24:35Z","body":"I don't think this is a bug. The ViewportTexture itself can be accessed fine; the error is because `get_image()` returns `null`, which per the docs it may do if the texture is invalid. The ViewportTexture for the root viewport doesn't have a `viewport_path` set, and the viewport won't have any internal reference to the duplicate you just made, so it makes sense to me that the duplicate would be invalid and not have any data on the GPU. You get the same result if you directly instantiate a new `Texture2D` or `ViewportTexture` and try to call `get_image()` on that.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3577841504/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]